---
intent: >
  Implement the aide_info MCP tool and wire the orchestrator boot sequence to
  detect stale host-side AIDE artifacts by comparing local versions against
  the canonical baseline.
---

## Plan

### 1. Create the aide_info tool module

Read: `coding-playbook/foundations/conventions`, `coding-playbook/architecture/folder-structure`

- [x] Create `src/tools/info/index.ts` with the tool's default export and Zod input schema
- [x] The module exports `InfoInput` (an empty Zod object — no parameters) as a named export, matching the pattern in `src/tools/discover/index.ts` and `src/tools/read/index.ts`
- [x] The default export is `async function info(): Promise<InfoResult>` — it takes no arguments (no `root`, no input params) since it only reads bundled package data, never host files
- [x] Import `readVersionsManifest` from `@/tools/upgrade/buildVersionsMeta/index.js` — reuse, do not duplicate
- [x] Read the server's own `package.json` version. Use `createRequire(import.meta.url)` to load the package.json from the installed package root (3 dirs up from `dist/tools/info/`), consistent with how `readVersionsManifest` resolves its path relative to the module location. Alternatively, use a `readFileSync` + `JSON.parse` approach mirroring `readVersionsManifest`. Do NOT use a dynamic `import()` for JSON — it requires import assertions that vary across Node versions
- [x] Return shape — define `InfoResult` interface in `src/types/index.ts`: `{ serverVersion: string; versions: VersionsMap }`. Import `VersionsMap` from its existing location in `@/tools/upgrade/buildVersionsMeta/index.js`
- [x] JSDoc on the default export explaining this is the passive staleness-detection surface called during orchestrator boot

### 2. Register aide_info in the MCP server

Read: `coding-playbook/foundations/conventions`, `coding-playbook/architecture/folder-structure`

- [x] In `src/index.ts`, add an import for the info tool: `import info, { InfoInput } from "@/tools/info/index.js";`
- [x] Add an `aide_info` entry to the `ListToolsRequestSchema` handler's tools array. Description: "Return the canonical AIDE versions manifest shipped with the server package and the server's npm version. Read-only, no parameters. The orchestrator calls this at boot to compare against the host project's local .aide/versions.json." Input schema: empty object (`type: "object", properties: {}`)
- [x] Add an `aide_info` case to the `CallToolRequestSchema` switch. Parse args with `InfoInput.parse(args)`, call `const result = await info()`, return `JSON.stringify(result, null, 2)` wrapped in the standard text content array — matching the aide_init/aide_upgrade JSON return pattern

